    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #308\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-112-module-contract-06-12-detect-live-mech-thr_8e3etcjz8r`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #112: registers `moduleRegistry.checkDrift`, a standalone heartbeat action that periodically detects live mechanical manifest drift that startup-time validation cannot catch:\n\n- Diffs distinct live `project_heartbeats.action_id` values against the registry's active heartbeat action ids.\n- Diffs distinct system-owned `properties.owner_process` values against active process/module ids.\n- Publishes findings through a resolve-capable extension of the existing `notifications` table (migration `0011_finding_resolution.sql` adds nullable `dedupe_key`/`resolved_at` columns plus a partial unique index on `(kind, dedupe_key) WHERE resolved_at IS NULL`).\n- Concurrent runs cannot create duplicate active findings (insert races safely resolve via `ON CONFLICT ... DO NOTHING`), and a repaired drift auto-resolves on the next successful run (`resolveFindingsNotIn`).\n- Deliberately mechanical only — never compares AGENT.md prose to permissions.\n\nNote: repo exploration showed this codebase's actual issue/commit history differs from the 12-part \"module-contract\" series description (no `ModuleManifest`/real module registry exists yet — that's intentionally deferred to issue #29). The implementation targets what's actually in the tree (`PermissionManifest`, `project_heartbeats`, `properties.owner_process`, the existing `core.driftCheck` action, which is left untouched) and adds this as a separate, additive check.\n\nVerified: `pnpm run build` (all 7 workspace packages compile) and `pnpm run test` (317/317 tests pass, including 4 new tests covering both drift checks, publish+resolve-on-repair, and concurrent-run dedup).\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
